# Raw response bodies are deliberately NOT committed.
# The five openid-configuration documents and the seven small control/404 bodies are the
# pass's evidence and are copied verbatim into ../openid/. The JWKS bodies are summarised in
# ../jwks-keys.json (kid/kty/alg/use) because each carries an RSA modulus and an x5c chain
# naming a vendor Auth0 custom domain. Raw bytes stay here so diff.py can re-derive
# ../verdict.txt on this machine; every byte is pinned by the sha256 in ../results.jsonl.
*
# CARVE-OUT (added 2026-10-12, round 4). The OPTIONS-phase and diagnostic bodies ARE
# committed, because they carry the load-bearing evidence of the /oidc/register
# retraction and none of them contains key material. Each is 0, 10 or 107 bytes of
# vendor error text: the empty bodies of the three 204 preflights, "Not found." from
# the absent-path controls, and the shadow tenants' "CORS error: Missing
# Access-Control-Request-Method header" JSON. No RSA modulus, no x5c, no certificate,
# no CN, no internal hostname -- verified before carving them out. Without these, the
# three-way 404 result and the wire-presence argument are not inspectable from a clean
# clone at all, which is the defect this carve-out exists to close.
!o01-*.b
!o02-*.b
!d1*.b
